  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Da vs Pawan Kumar Goel on 6 July, 2018 In The Court Of Samar Vishal, Additional Chief Metropolitan Magistrate, Patiala House Courts, New Delhi Cc No. 39044/2016 Date of Institution : 19.12.2002 Date of reserving judgement : 05.07.2018 Date of pronouncement : 06.07.2018 In re: Delhi Administration / Food Inspector Department of Pfa, Govt. of Nct of Delhi A-20, Lawrence Road Industrial Area, Delhi-110035 ... Complainant versus A-1) Sh. Pawan Kumar Goel, S/o Sh. Suraj Prakash Goel M/s Pawan Kumar Gaurav Kumar, Shop No. 162, Devli Road, Village Devli, New Delhi - 62 R/o H No. 162, Devli Road Village Devli, New Delhi - 62 A-2) Mukesh Kumar Mittal S/o Late Sh Desh Raj Mittal M/s Shyam Lal Raj Kumar, 4053-55, Naya Bazar, Delhi ... 1. The present is a complaint filed under section 16 of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act, 1954 (herein after referred to Da vs Pawan Kumar Goel as Pfa Act), alleging that the accused have viola",
    "facts": "1. The present is a complaint filed under section 16 of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act, 1954 (herein after referred to Da vs Pawan Kumar Goel as Pfa Act), alleging that the accused have viola ted the provisions of the PFA Act and Rules. 2. As per the complaint, on 13.03.2002 the Food Inspector C.B. Boora purchased a sample of 'Arhar Dal\" a food article for analysis from accused Pawan Kumar Goel at M/s Pawan Kumar Gaurav Kumar, Shop No. 162, Devli Road, Village Devli, New Delhi - 62, where the said food article was found stored for sale and where accused No.1 Pawan Kumar Goel was found conducting the business of the said food article at the time of sampling. The sample consisted 750 gms of Arhar Dal Da vs Pawan Kumar Goel on 6 July, 2018 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/78487250/ 1 taken from an open gunny bag bearing no label declaration. The sample was taken under the supervision / direction of Sh. A.K. Singh, SDM/LHA (Kalkaji). The sample was taken after mixing the Arhar Dal by rotating it with the help of clean and dry jhaba several times in all possible directions. The Food Inspector divided the sample then and there into three equal parts by putting them in three separate clean and dry bottles. Each bottle was separately packed, fastened and sealed according to PFA Act and Rules. The vendor's signatures were obtained on the LHA slip and the wrapper of the sample bottles. Notice was given to accused No. 1 Pawan Kumar Goel and the price of sample was also given to him vide vendor receipt dated 13.03.2002. Panchnama too was prepared at the spot. All the documents prepared by F.I. were signed by accused No.1 Pawan Kumar Goel and the other witness Sh Satish Kumar Gupta, FI, Before starting sample proceeding efforts were made to join public witnesses but none came forward, as such Sh Satish Kumar Gupta , FI was joined as witness. DA vs Pawan Kumar Goel 3. One counter-part of the sample bearing LHA code No. AKS/LHA/001546 was also sent to Public Analyst, Delhi in intact condition and two counter-parts were deposited with the LHA in intact condition. Public Analyst analysed the sample and found the same to be adulterated. The report of the Public Analyst is as follows: \"The sample is adulterated because it is coloured with synthetic colouring matter viz tartarzine.\" 4. It is the case of the complainant that accused No.1 Pawan Kumar Goel was the vendor-cum-proprietor of M/s Pawan Kumar Gaurav Kumar, Shop No. 162, Devli Road, Village Devli, New Delhi - 62, at the time of sampling and as such he was incharge of and responsible for day to day conduct of the business of the said shop. 5. Thereafter on completion of investigation, sanction under section 20 of the PFA Act was obtained from the Director PFA. The complaint was then filed in the court on 19.12.2002 alleging violation of section 2(ia)(j)&(m) and Rule 23 read with Rule 28 & 29 of PFA Rules, 1955 as punishable section 7/16(1)(a) of PFA Act against the accused. During the trial, vide order dated 22.12.2009 accused No. 2 Mukesh Kumar Mittal was also impleaded in this case as an accused. 6. As the complaint was filed in writing by a public servant, recording of pre-summoning evidence was dispensed with and the accused was summoned vide order dated 19.12.2002. The accused DA vs Pawan Kumar Goel thereafter exercised their option of analysing the counter part through CFL under section 13 (2) of the PFA Act. Based on the report of the CFL as well as evidence led in pre charge evidence, charge was framed against the accused for commission of the offence punishable under section 7/16(1) (a) PFA Act being violation of Section 2(ia)(j)&(m) of PFA Act and Rule 23 read with Rule 28 & 29 of PFA Rules, 1955, to which accused person pleaded not guilty and claimed trial. Da vs Pawan Kumar Goel on 6 July, 2018 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/78487250/ 2 7. At the trial, the prosecution examined four witness in support of its case i.e. PW-1 SDM/LHA Sh A.K. Singh, PW-2 FI C.B. Boora, PW-3 FI Rajpal Singh, PW-4 FI Satish Kumar Gupta. PW-2 C.B. Boora and PW-4 FI Satish Kumar Gupta were part of the team that had visited the spot for sample proceedings under the supervision of SDM/LHA Sh. A.K. Singh. These witness narrated the steps undertaken by them during the sample proceedings, including disclosing their identity, expressing intention to purchase sample for analysis, lifting the sample commodity of \"Arhar Dal \" 750 gms from the vendor for analysis, bearing no label or declaration, taking the sample of Arhar Dal and mixing help of a clean & dry jhaba, dividing the sample into three equal parts by putting them into three separate clean and dry sample bottles, separately sealing, packing and marking the same and obtaining signatures of vendor and witnesses. They also proved the necessary documents including the vendor's receipt Ex.PW-1/A, Notice Ex. PW-1/B, Panchnama Ex.PW-1/C. The accused also made statement Ex.PW1/D alongwith document Ex.PW2/A. Thereafter, on 14.03.2002 one counterpart of the sample along with one copy of memo in form VII and another copy of memo in DA vs Pawan Kumar Goel form VII in sealed deposited with PA vide receipt Ex.PW2/B. The remaining two counter parts of the sample in intact condition along with two copies of memo of Form VII in a sealed packet were deposited with LHA vide LHA Receipt Ex.PW1/E under intimation that one counterpart of the same has already been deposited with PA. Thereafter, PA Report Ex.PW1/F was received, according to which the sample was adulterated because the same was coloured with synthetic colouring matter tatrazin. Thereafter PW-2 C.B. Boora conducted further investigation and collected reply from STO vide Ex.PW1/G. After completion of investigation, the entire case file was put before then Director PFA for obtaining his Consent. The then Director PFA granted his Consent for prosecution vide sanction order Ex.PW1/H. Thereafter, the present complaint Ex.PW1/J was filed before the Court. Then intimation letter Ex.PW1/K alongwith copy of PA Reports was sent to the accused vide postal receipt Ex.PW1/L. These witnesses were duly cross-examined by Ld. Defence Counsel. 8. Statement of the accused under section 313 CrPC were recorded wherein the accused persons denied the allegations and pleaded innocence. Thereafter matter was listed for defence evidence. 9. In their defence, the accused No. 2 Mukesh Kumar Mittal and accused No. 1 Pawan Kumar Goel examined themselves as DW-1 and DW-3. The accused also examined one Sunil Kumar Gupta and Raghubir Saran as DW-2 and DW-4. Thereafter defence evidence was closed vide order dated 01.07.2016 and the matter was fixed for final arguments.",
    "arguments": "Muralidhar Shyamlal v. State of Assam [1996(I) PFA Cases 86].",
